1. Converse's RUN_ERROR carries rawEvent (toRunErrorRawEvent), as the other
   adapters' do since TanStack/ai#985; it had none, so the provider status was
   lost. Upstream PR to be opened. Remove when an @tanstack/ai-bedrock release
   does it.
2. The terminal event carries messageStop's stopReason as
   metadata.providerStopReason (null when the stream ended without one), so the
   service decides every stop reason from the SDK's StopReason union
   (apps/api/src/lib/chat/provider-stop-reasons.ts). Remove when upstream
   exposes the raw reason.

